# Line endings are part of the build output.
#
# `apps/studio/dist/client.bundle.js` is built on macOS, Linux AND Windows
# runners, and the release asserts all three produce the artifact that was
# reviewed. With no policy here, Git for Windows checks sources out as CRLF
# (core.autocrlf defaults to true there), so the Windows runner bundles
# different bytes than everyone else — measured at 385 bytes on 2026-08-02,
# after pinning Bun and committing apps/studio/bun.lock had made macOS and
# Linux agree exactly.
#
# Normalizing to LF in the working tree on every platform removes the last
# input that varies by who is building.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, or byte-exact by contract — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.webm binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.bundle binary
*.kuzu binary

# The committed build outputs. They are compared byte-for-byte against what CI
# builds, so any conversion at all would break the comparison it exists for.
apps/studio/dist/** -text
